  "text": "[calm] How does a cue reach inside a room? Deck and room are pages from the same origin, so the deck can simply reach in — no protocol, no messages — if the room offers something to hold. [short pause] That something is a hook: a few lines added to a room, naming what it already knows how to do. The deck calls the hook; the hook presses the room's own buttons. [short pause] The smallest hook in the estate is one line — fifty-seven bytes. It stops the museum's timelapse and shows the age you ask for. [pause] And you may have noticed the sun is setting. This room's hook runs the same glide as its own sunset button. I cued it a few sentences ago — on the word \"reach.\"",
